<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-924] addEntry() is susceptible to spurious wakeups</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-924</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;LedgerHandle sync interface heavily depends on SyncCounter to convert async interfaces&lt;br/&gt;
into sync interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Usaylly&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SyncCounter.inc()&lt;br/&gt;
asyncCall()&lt;br/&gt;
SyncCOunter.block(0)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The block code is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;   synchronized void block(int limit) throws InterruptedException {&lt;br/&gt;
        while (i &amp;gt; limit) {&lt;br/&gt;
            int prev = i;&lt;br/&gt;
            wait();&lt;br/&gt;
            if (i == prev) &lt;/p&gt;
{
                break;
            }
&lt;p&gt;        }&lt;br/&gt;
    }&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since &apos;i&apos; is going to be same as &apos;prev&apos; on spurious wakeup, and wait() can return on spurious wakeups. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
